 You can instantly upload your project to Vercel by selecting the default HUGO configuration, but depending on your own tech stack whether it's React.js, Vue, Nuxt.js, Next.js or a back-end framework you can also just copy the layouts from this project inside your own tech stack.
 
+[![Deploy to Wasmer](https://img.shields.io/badge/Deploy%20to-Wasmer-171717?logo=wasmer&logoColor=white)](https://wasmer.io/apps/create?github=themesberg%2Fflowbite-admin-dashboard)
+
+You can also deploy it on Wasmer: the included `Anybuild` file runs `npm install`, the webpack build and Hugo with `--baseURL=/` (so links and assets point to your Wasmer URL rather than the `baseURL` in `config.yml`), then serves the generated `public/` folder as static files. The button opens Wasmer's import page for this public repository, where you review the detected settings (and correct them if needed) before clicking Deploy; nothing is deployed until you do. It does not create a copy of the repository in your GitHub account. To customize the dashboard, fork the repository and import your fork instead.
+
